And add a toggle for dark mode with a radio button input in the HTML:
```html
<input id="dark-mode-toggle" type="radio" checked>
```
Don't forget to add a label and a change listener to the radio input to toggle the dark mode class:
```css
#dark-mode-toggle:checked ~ #dark-mode-toggle-label {
  transform: rotate(180deg);
}
```
```html
<label for="dark-mode-toggle" id="dark-mode-toggle-label">Toggle Dark Mode</label>
```
```javascript
document.querySelector('#dark-mode-toggle').addEventListener('change', () => {
  document.body.classList.toggle('dark-mode');
});
```
Now you'll need to add a CSS class for dark mode and use the same classes and styles from the light mode version with simply CSS class switching:
```css
body.dark-mode {
  background-color: #1a1a1a;
  color: #fff;
}
```
